<!-- @diagram 2301ffe70d644897 -->
### Who talks to whom

<figure class="viz"><div class="viz-stack"><div class="node"><strong><code>LazyColumn</code></strong><small>reports scrolling; renders <code>PagingData</code></small></div><div class="down"></div><div class="node is-key"><strong><code>Pager</code> (in the ViewModel)</strong><small>reads pages from the database; triggers the mediator when they run out</small></div><div class="viz-grid" style="--cols:2"><div class="node" data-state="done"><strong>Room database</strong><small>source of every page the UI sees</small></div><div class="node"><strong><code>RemoteMediator</code></strong><small>fetches from the network API and inserts into Room</small></div></div></div><figcaption>The UI never talks to the network; it only observes the database through a PagingSource.</figcaption></figure>

<!-- @after Staff Engineer Thinking :: check -->
**Which fix?** Decide before opening each answer.

<details><summary>The list jumps back to the top after every rotation.</summary>

The `Pager` flow is not cached. Apply `cachedIn(viewModelScope)` in the ViewModel so the new UI collects the same paged data.
</details>

<details><summary>New posts at the top of the server feed cause duplicates further down.</summary>

Offset pagination shifted under the user. Use a cursor key from the server so continuation does not depend on positions.
</details>

<details><summary>Refresh briefly shows an empty list before the new data.</summary>

Clearing and inserting happened in separate transactions. Do both inside one `withTransaction` so invalidation never observes the empty table.
</details>

